Derek Ray wrote:

> The optimal path for ascension does not lead
> through pudding farming, but then again, that
> isn't the issue at hand, is it?

But then, what IS the issue?

No, really; I've seen your arguments that it is some
blemish on the game because it is a source of nearly
infinite goodies, but, *so what*?

Potion alchemy was _added to the game_ to be a
source of ridiculously many hitpoints and wishes,
nurse dancing and foocubi dalliance allow ridiculous
values to show up on status lines as well, and they
both were _added_ with that intention.

"Monty Haul" is a firmly embedded part of the
dungeon crawl player mentality, it isn't going to go
away if pudding farming gets nerfed.

On the open and public servers, even ascending won't
guarantee you a place in the saved record file
despite it being 2000 entries long instead of 100
entries long as on a personal computer.

If pudding farming is suboptimal play anyway, and
Rider farming is a much less painful way to roll the
score counter for the *Big Score* addicts, why does
pudding farming in particular need to come out of
the game?

Just because some few, vociferous players find it
offensive, should it go, when it seems many more
players find it a fun, if occasional, diversion from
normal game play?

We notice that yipping about "evil pudding farming"
in particular misses out that there was a posting
today about farming vampire bats on a quest, that
there are frequent postings about altar camping.

Players who _want_ to build huge stacks of death
drops will _find_ a way, even if it is playing
extinctionist. What's the big deal that makes
pudding farming _in particular_ such a huge target
to a few deranged-obsessive rgrn poster-people, when
it has no competitive aspect of significance to
anyone, anyway?

Has any one of the whiners about pudding farming
ever been _hurt_ by someone else's playing a game
with pudding farming as a component, except perhaps
by inheriting a bones file that was "too rich" or
"too dangerous"?

Has that happened to any one person often enough for
all the whining that results?

Get a grip, people.

Quantum valeat.

